# dev-ios scope

**iOS-only (Simulator / XcodeBuildMCP):** `ios-workflow.mdc`, `xcode-mcp-only.mdc` (Simulator/Shell bypass bar), **XcodeBuildMCP**, and skills `build-ios-apps`, `ios-*`.

**macOS and iOS (Xcode open):** **`xcode-tools` MCP** — docs, Issue Navigator, `GetBuildLog`, `RenderPreview`, optional `BuildProject` / tests in the open Xcode window. Hooks **never** block `xcode-tools` outside iOS scope; agents may use it on macOS-only projects.

**Cross-platform SwiftUI skills:** `swiftui-ui-patterns`, `swiftui-view-refactor`, `swiftui-performance-audit`, `swiftui-liquid-glass`.

## Active when any workspace root has one of:

- `.xcodebuildmcp/config.yaml` (XcodeBuildMCP host setup)
- `.cursor/dev-ios` (explicit opt-in)
- An Xcode `project.pbxproj` with iOS targets (`iphoneos` / `iphonesimulator` / `TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY`)

## Inactive otherwise

Examples: macOS-only `.xcodeproj`, Swift packages with no iOS platform, Node/Python repos, or Xcode projects with only `SDKROOT = macosx`.

When **inactive**:

- Ignore `ios-workflow.mdc` and `xcode-mcp-only.mdc`; do not use XcodeBuildMCP or require `build_sim`.
- Hooks block **XcodeBuildMCP** and **iOS-only** skills/scripts listed above. **`xcode-tools` stays allowed.**
- Shell `xcodebuild`, `xcrun`, and normal Xcode/CLI builds are allowed.
- Do not tell the user that ios-workflow forbids Shell; that restriction applies only when this scope is **active**.

Opt out on a mixed repo: add `.cursor/dev-ios-off` at the workspace root.
